<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the Fed to refrain from action.</p>
<p>At 1132 EDT/1532 GMT, federal funds were trading at 5-1/8 percent, below the central bank's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679</p>
